semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 相敬如宾 specifically characterizes married couples treating one another with dignified courtesy, mutual deference, and unflagging decorum.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 相敬如宾 vs. 举案齐眉 | jǔ'ànqíméi | Both describe marital respect, but 举案齐眉 historically highlighted the wife's dutiful deference to the husband, whereas 相敬如宾 emphasizes symmetrical, mutual respect between both partners.
    2 | 相敬如宾 vs. 恩爱如初 | ēn'àirúchū | 恩爱如初 emphasizes the undiminished emotional passion and affection of early romance, while 相敬如宾 emphasizes polite restraint, decorum, and mutual reverence.
    3 | 相敬如宾 vs. 亲密无间 | qīnmìwújiàn | 亲密无间 denotes boundless casual intimacy without formalities, whereas 相敬如宾 maintains a respectful, courteous boundary to avoid domestic contempt.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 中国古人将相敬如宾视为夫妻相处的最高境界。爱情最初由激情点燃，但要在数十年的柴米油盐中免于厌倦，唯有以礼相待。将伴侣视作尊贵的宾客，言语有度，举止有礼，才能让婚姻在岁月流转中沉淀出温润的优雅。 | Zhōngguó gǔrén jiāng xiāngjìngrúbīn shìwéi fūqī xiāngchǔ de zuìgāo jìngjiè. Àiqíng zuìchū yóu jīqíng diǎnrán, dàn yào zài shù shí nián de cháimǐyóuyán zhōng miǎnyú yànjuàn, wéiyǒu yǐ lǐ xiāng dài. Jiāng bànlǚ shìzuò zūnguì de bīnkè, yányǔ yǒudù, jǔzhǐ yǒulǐ, cáinǐng ràng hūnyīn zài suìyuè liúzhuǎn zhōng chéndiàn chū wēnrùn de yōuyǎ. | Ancient Chinese regarded mutual respect like guests as the summit of matrimony. Passion kindles love, but avoiding domestic weariness over decades requires courtesy. Treating your partner as an honored guest allows marriage to distill gentle elegance over time. | Los antiguos concebían el respeto mutuo como la cúspide conyugal. La pasión enciende el amor, pero para sortear el tedio cotidiano durante décadas se precisa cortesía. Considerar al cónyuge como un huésped de honor destila una serena elegancia matrimonial.
  #2 | 在现代文化语境中，相敬如宾这一传统成语常被赋予关于婚姻边界感的新内涵。现代家庭咨询顾问指出，过度亲昵往往容易模糊彼此的心理界限，引发不必要的控制欲。保持如宾客般的相互尊重与独立空间，是构建健康伙伴式婚姻的重要法则。 | Zài xiàndài wénhuà yǔjìng zhōng, xiāngjìngrúbīn zhè yì chuántǒng chéngyǔ cháng bèi fùyǔ guānyú hūnyīn biānjiègǎn de xīn nèihán. Xiàndài jiātíng zīxún gùwèn zhǐchū, guòdù qīnnì wǎngwǎng róngyì móhu bǐcǐ de xīnlǐ jièxiàn, yǐnfā búbìyào de kòngzhìyù. Bǎochí rú bīnkè bān de xiānghù zūnzhòng yǔ dúlì kōngjiān, shì gòujiàn jiànkāng huǒbànshì hūnyīn de zhòngyào fǎzé. | In contemporary contexts, respecting each other like guests gains new meaning around marital psychological boundaries. Counselors note that unchecked familiarity blurs boundaries and fuels possessiveness. Preserving courteous space is a vital rule for healthy partnership marriage. | En la psicología contemporánea, respetarse como huéspedes cobra nuevo sentido sobre los límites personales en la pareja. La excesiva confianza borra las fronteras afectivas y alienta el afán de control. Mantener un espacio de respeto mutuo forja una convivencia sana y equilibrada.
